From 2c3400aa9f397da48a6760f5e84438973e01a00c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:38:08 +0700
Subject: ASoC: amd: acp: Fix .close() being skipped on rollback
Git-commit: 2c3400aa9f397da48a6760f5e84438973e01a00c
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

snd_pcm_hw_constraint_integer() may return 1, which is then returned
from acp_dma_open(). ASoC only marks the component as opened when
.open() returns 0, so .close() can be skipped on rollback.

Return 0 explicitly on success.

Fixes: 623621a9f9e1 ("ASoC: amd: Add common framework to support I2S on ACP SOC")
Signed-off-by: bui duc phuc <phucduc.bui@gmail.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261008103831.542533-2-phucduc.bui@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 sound/soc/amd/acp/acp-platform.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/sound/soc/amd/acp/acp-platform.c
+++ b/sound/soc/amd/acp/acp-platform.c
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ static int acp_dma_open(struct snd_soc_c
 	list_add_tail(&stream->list, &adata->stream_list);
 	spin_unlock_irq(&adata->acp_lock);
 
-	return ret;
+	return 0;
 }
 
 static int acp_dma_hw_params(struct snd_soc_component *component,
